---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="DMCA Policy - YTools"
  description="YTools DMCA (Digital Millennium Copyright Act) compliance policy and takedown request process."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 w-full">
    <div class="glass-panel rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-10 space-y-6 text-text-main">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">DMCA Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Last updated: {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</p>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Copyright Compliance</h2>
        <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
          YTools respects the intellectual property rights of others and expects its users to do the same.
          We comply with the Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA) and respond to valid notices of
          alleged copyright infringement.
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
          All tools process files locally in your browser. We do not host, store, or transmit user files
          or third-party content on our servers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. Filing a Takedown Notice</h2>
        <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
          If you believe that your copyrighted work has been used in a way that constitutes copyright
          infringement, please send a written notice that includes the following information:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-text-muted pl-2">
          <li>A description of the copyrighted work you claim has been infringed.</li>
          <li>The URL or a description of where the allegedly infringing material is located.</li>
          <li>Your name, address, telephone number, and email address.</li>
          <li>A statement that you have a good-faith belief that the use is not authorized.</li>
          <li>A statement, made under penalty of perjury, that the information in your notice is accurate and that you are the copyright owner or authorized to act on their behalf.</li>
          <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Send all DMCA takedown notices and copyright inquiries to our designated agent:
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary-500">lwj619862787@gmail.com</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Counter-Notification</h2>
        <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
          If you believe your content was removed in error, you may submit a counter-notification. It must
          include your contact information, a description of the removed material, a statement under penalty
          of perjury that you have a good-faith belief the material was removed by mistake, and your consent
          to the jurisdiction of your local federal court.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted border-t border-black/10 dark:border-white/10 pt-4">
        This policy is provided as a general template and does not constitute legal advice. Please review it
        with a qualified attorney to ensure it meets your specific obligations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
